// Local signing configuration — copy to Tacendum.xcconfig (same directory,
// gitignored) and fill in. The copy is the setup step; this file is the schema.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The Apple Developer Team ID used to be a literal in
// project.pbxproj. It is not a secret, but it fails .env.example's test for
// what may stay in the repository — "is it already public by another route?"
// A Team ID is not: it names the legal entity behind the app and is one of
// the two identifiers an Apple-support social-engineering attempt starts
// from. So it lives here, next to the project, in a file git never sees.
//
// HOW IT IS WIRED. This file is the base configuration of the two
// PROJECT-level build configurations. That placement is load-bearing:
// CocoaPods owns the TARGET-level base configurations (Pods-*.xcconfig per
// target and configuration), and attaching this file there would detach the
// Pods ones and break the build. The project level had no base configuration
// at all, targets inherit from it, and `pod install` never touches it. The
// four DEVELOPMENT_TEAM settings in project.pbxproj are the reference
// $(TACENDUM_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM), resolved from here.
//
// SUPERSEDED — READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE FILE BESIDE IT.
//
// This example used to describe a scheme where Tacendum.xcconfig itself was
// gitignored, and asserted that a missing file left Simulator builds working
// while only device builds failed. That was false, and the way it was
// "verified" is the lesson: `xcodebuild -showBuildSettings` tolerates a
// missing base-configuration reference and exits 0; `xcodebuild build` does
// not. A clean clone could not build the app or the extension at all.
//
// Today `Tacendum.xcconfig` is COMMITTED with an empty default and an
// optional include, and the file you create locally is
// `Tacendum.local.xcconfig`. Copy THAT:
//
//     cp app/ios/Tacendum.xcconfig.example app/ios/Tacendum.local.xcconfig
//     # then set TACENDUM_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM to the team's ID
//
// The rationale for keeping the value out of git is unchanged and still
// correct — a Team ID names the legal entity and is one of two identifiers
// an Apple-support social-engineering attempt starts from. What changed is
// that the FILE no longer has to be withheld to withhold the VALUE.

// Apple Developer Team ID (developer.apple.com → Membership).
// Push only works when this is the team the server's APNs key is scoped
// to: a build signed by a different team gets tokens Apple will not
// accept for that key.
TACENDUM_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
